{"name":"Wahl clippers","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_%2851013604297%29.jpg/960px-Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_%2851013604297%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_(51013604297).jpg","caption":"Hair Clipper - Wahl (51013604297)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Wahl is an American grooming-tools company founded in 1921 and best known for hair clippers and beard trimmers. Its clippers are common in barbershops and homes.","They help looks by letting people keep a short cut, fade or neat beard outline without regular barber visits. T Nation forum users have recommended Wahl, with one saying most barbers use it."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Users fit guard combs to buzz the head or blend a fade, and use a smaller trimmer for lines and beards, usually starting on a longer guard. Forum posters describe cutting every two to three weeks."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Minimal; nicks or uneven cuts from clippers and irritation are the usual concerns. Wahl is one of several brands (forum users also name Oster and Andis)."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_%2851013604297%29.jpg/960px-Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_%2851013604297%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_%2851013604297%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hair Clipper - Wahl (51013604297)","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"ajay_suresh","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hair_Clipper_-_Wahl_(51013604297).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/WAHL_Pet_Cli