hl_Clipper"},{"title":"Wahl Clipper Corporation - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wahl_Clipper_Corporation"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Grooming","chain":["Buy a clipper and guards","Cut or fade hair and trim beard at home","Neat, consistent haircut between visits"],"effect":"direct","text":"A home clipper keeps hair or beard at a chosen length and shape, including buzz cuts and fades. Some users also use clippers to shorten body hair."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Wahl Clipper","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wahl_Clipper"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Wahl Clipper Corporation, based in Sterling, Illinois, was incorporated in 1921 after Leo J. Wahl patented an electromagnetic clipper in 1919.[1] It later introduced a vibrating-motor clipper (1924), a vacuum clipper (1965), a cordless rechargeable clipper (1966) and cordless beard trimmers (1984).[1]","Men on T Nation have recommended Wahl for self-cutting, with one writing that they use Wahl \"as do most barbers\", and others pairing a Wahl clipper with an Andis trimmer for fade and line-up.[2][3] Posters also describe a cheap clipper as a way to shave or buzz a thinning head.[4]"],"infobox":[["Type","Hair clippers and trimmers"],["Company","Wahl Clipper Corporation"],["Founded","1921"],["Headquarters","Sterling, Illinois"],["Brands","Wahl, Moser, Lister, Groom Ease"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["Leo J. Wahl patented a clipper in 1919 and bought his uncle's company stock in 1921.[1] Later milestones included the first cordless rechargeable clipper in 1966, the acquisition of Moser in 1996 and a home-haircutting line in 2006.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing communities","paras":["T Nation posters recommend Wahl for self-cutting, buzz cuts and fades, and for trimming chest hair to a short length for a better appearance.[2][3][5]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1919","event":"Leo J. Wahl patents an electromagnetic c